  "conclusion": "corresponds",
  "rationale": "Destructor extension author review. StackTyping.ConfigurationTyped combines class/declaration well-formedness, StackShape, and Shared Realizes with empty variable environment and occurrence-preserving roots from all frames. BodyFrom includes Finished after ResultTyped; suspended ContinuationTyped checks result delivery before the caller remainder. Shared realization includes nominal field correctness and reference view/mode observations, even on hidden fields. RetainsClasses quantifies over all raw-heap entries whose nominal kind is not struct, requiring the same entry in the collected heap; it does not forbid explicit unpacking in the raw operation. The text distinguishes the collector obligation from heap realization. Rooted-foundation review: the structural invariants now require explicit rootedness (including pending values) plus unique/compatible ownership. Allocation bounds remain solely for freshness; no safety proof assumes edge-age order or global DAG structure. Changed proof selections retain their public statement unless this unit explicitly defines the revised invariant or example. Given/Shared root transport and path reasoning were reviewed by their implementing agents, with fresh review of root-owned unpacking, GC, frame rerooting, class retention and the refill example. Earlier syntax and runtime rules are unchanged. The widened invariant domain is covered by recompilation of all earlier safety proofs and concrete shared-cycle/nonmonotonic-ID regressions, not by a claim that constructors can generate cycles.",
  "limitations": [
    "Author integration review with agent review of Given/Shared foundations and fresh review of root-owned integration. Lean checks proof correctness separately.",
    "Assignment general safety remains deferred. Cyclic heap examples test invariant and operation scope, not source-program construction from the current empty initial state."
  ],
